  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to Humanitarian Needs - Analysis and Assessment - Joint Intersectoral Analysis Framework (JIAF) 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian needs have risen drastically over the last decade, but international funding for humanitarian assistance has not kept pace. The international humanitarian community has called for more informed needs-assessments in order to make efficient use of the humanitarian funding available. To respond to the advocacy of the international humanitarian sector, experienced humanitarian partners have come together to develop the Joint Intersectoral Analysis Framework (JIAF), a new approach to analyzing humanitarian needs. The JIAF is managed by IOM. The expected outcomes of this project include: 1) improved high-quality needs analysis to inform humanitarian response plans, as well as other strategic response plans; 2) strengthened humanitarian capacity to more effectively meet the needs of populations affected by crises; and 3) improved prioritization of humanitarian donor resources to reach those most in need.</narrative>
  </description>
